# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Dohyeong Kwon et al. (2024). Machine learning interatomic potentials in engineering perspective for developing cathode materials.
#   Journal of Materials Chemistry A. doi:10.1039/d4ta03452j
#
# Version read: publisher (sha256 8a1458d7200c452b...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 198 (Overview/taxonomy). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. The article is a perspective
# with a feasibility study: the pretrained universal potentials CHGNet
# (version 0.3.0) and M3GNet (via MatGL) are applied to cathode materials
# and compared with DFT (VASP, PBE) for voltages, energy rankings of
# Li configurations and lattice parameters during delithiation. It
# trains no model and reports no energy, force or stress error of a test
# set.

